 for Many-core Systems. In: 10th International Conference on Electrical Systems, 2-4 April 2014, KLCC, Kuala Lumpur. (Submitted)
Full text not available from this repository.
Real-time scheduling and routing are two essential and inter-related issues for hard-real-time (HRT) Embedded Networks-on-chip (NoC). The routing policies in the underlying network infrastructure play a major part in deciding whether a set of tasks scheduled according to a certain strategy (i.e., Earliest Deadline First (EDF) or Deadlines First (DF) strategy for tasks execution) can be executed correctly according to the time constraint. Hence, this paper presents a joint optimization technique for early exploration and selection of the appropriate combination of routing policies, scheduling algorithms and communication parameters for hard-realtime many-core (HRTMC) systems, considering the performance and timing constraint. As part of the design space exploration (DSE), a number of HRT task sets are generated

